Subject: [PATCH] spi: geni-qcom: leave successful DMA messages in progress

spi_transfer_one_message checks msg->status before adding actual_length.
The callback must preserve -EINPROGRESS on success, otherwise the core exits
before accounting the bytes. Only publish failures from the callback.

This is the small status-accounting fix also present in the pending series:
https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/11/06/2331
The larger transfer_one_message/QSPI refactor is not needed here.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -400,8 +400,9 @@
 	struct spi_controller *spi = cb;
 	struct spi_geni_master *mas = spi_controller_get_devdata(spi);
 
-	spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
+	/* The SPI core finalizes successful messages after accounting the transfer. */
 	if (result->result != DMA_TRANS_NOERROR) {
+		spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
 		dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA txn failed: %d\n", result->result);
 		trace_geni_se_regs(&mas->se);
 		spi_finalize_current_transfer(spi);
@@ -409,9 +410,9 @@
 	}
 
 	if (!result->residue) {
-		spi->cur_msg->status = 0;
 		dev_dbg(&spi->dev, "DMA txn completed\n");
 	} else {
+		spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
 		dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA xfer has pending: %d\n", result->residue);
 		trace_geni_se_regs(&mas->se);
 	}
